name w3-02-net-intact-1
timeout 700
time 1991-01-17T00:00:00Z

# CAMPAIGN W3, SORTIE 2 OF 10 - THE SAME NIGHT WITH THE EARLY-WARNING SET LEFT ALIVE.
# Spec, anchor and sources: doc/campaigns/w3-desert-storm.md. Format: doc/missions/campaign.md.
# CONTROL: this file IS the controlled variant. Its control is w3-01-ew-radar.fbm.
# THE ONE TOKEN THAT DIFFERS: `set brief_master_arm arm` -> `sim` on the first striker. Everything
# else - route, altitude, speed, load-out, clock, net, battery magazines, the second wave's whole plan -
# is the control's, line for line. The SMS then rejects the pickle (`hardware_precedence`, master arm
# not in ARM) and the P-18 lives.
#
# THE CAST IS PAIRWISE DISJOINT FROM SORTIE 01'S IN EVERY UNIT IT CAN LOSE, aircraft AND GROUND
# (`q2*`, `k2*` against `q1*`, `kari*`). That is O5's rule and it is not optional here: sortie 01 is the
# head of this campaign's carry chain, so a shared ground callsign would arrive in this file already
# destroyed and there would be no control left. The two files are compared with the callsign prefix
# normalised, which is exactly what the campaign's State section does.
#
# THE ARENA, the net-as-buried-cable, the three substitutions and their direction, and what NIGHT is
# worth in this tree are all stated in w3-01-ew-radar.fbm and hold unchanged here.
#
# WHICH DEFENSIVE LAYER THIS FILE MEASURES: the MISSILE layer, with no fighter in it.
#
# THE ONE TACTICAL QUESTION: WHAT DOES AN INTACT EARLY-WARNING NODE COST THE AIRCRAFT BEHIND IT? Not
# "does the ring shoot" - that is a mechanism and w3-01 already shows it working - but the price in the
# only currency a strike campaign has: STRIKERS THAT REACHED RELEASE. The second F-16 flies the identical
# route in both files; here the ring is awake when it arrives.
#
# THE ANSWER IS NOT A SHOOT-DOWN, AND THAT IS THE INTERESTING PART. MEASURED (fingerprint
# 2b7bb7d497a4dde8): the one token is visible in the log as `sms RELEASE_REJECTED ... reason=
# hardware_precedence detail="master arm not in ARM"` at t = 70.4, on the same tick the control
# released. The S-125 then fires four V-601 (t = 340.7 / 343.2 / 373.9 / 376.4, from 28.1 / 27.5 / 20.8
# / 20.2 km) which arrive at 8.35, 8.17, 7.28 and 7.42 m against a 10 m fuze; `q2pen` is NOT killed -
# it flies on and its `survive` objective is met - but the FIRST arrival fails eleven systems at once,
# `stores` among them, at t = 392.4 s. It reaches its aim point at t = 448.3 s, 55.9 s later, with a
# dead SMS, and drops nothing. `k2dra` ends the run INTACT. The S-75 then empties its own six rounds at
# the departing aircraft (brgDeg 102-111, i.e. east) and hits nothing.
# THAT IS SUPPRESSION OF THE ATTACKER, measured as a system failure and not as a loss, and it is the
# quantity the campaign contract asks every W3 mission to report.
#
# THE FULL COMPARISON AGAINST ITS CONTROL:
#   quantity                        w3-01 (node dead)     w3-02 (node alive)
#   `site LAUNCH`                   0                     10  (S-125 x4, S-75 x6)
#   `stores DETONATION` on a jet    0                     4   (7.28 - 8.35 m)
#   strikers reaching release       2 of 2                0 of 2 - one was refused its pickle by the
#                                                         one token, the other lost its SMS 56 s short
#   ground targets destroyed        `karinod`, `kariref`  none
#   run length                      700.0 s (timeout)     700.0 s (timeout)
#
# ATTRIBUTION (rule 4 - this result has two possible causes and gets a control run, not an argument).
# The un-armed striker never releases, so it also never flies the 135 deg attack egress: its path after
# t = 70 s differs from the control's. ATTRIBUTION RUN A1 deletes `q2str` from this file entirely and
# flies `q2pen` alone against the same live net. The belt's behaviour is reported in
# doc/campaigns/w3-desert-storm.md, State, and the run does NOT come out neutral - which is why rule 4
# exists. Without the un-armed striker the belt fires 8 instead of 10 and `q2pen` is SHOT DOWN (FAIL at
# t = 358.9) instead of surviving with a dead SMS. So a striker that never dropped anything, 95 km
# west of every fire unit, was nevertheless worth two rounds and its wingman's life: A FLIGHTBOX
# BATTERY HAS NO IFF INTERROGATOR AND NO THREAT PRIORITY, and it splits a finite magazine over
# whatever is in reach. The same mechanism decides sorties 04 and 05.
#
# WHAT TO READ:
#   events.log      `sms RELEASE_REJECTED ... master arm not in ARM` at t = 70.4 (the one token, visible),
#                   then the `site LAUNCH` block, `damage SYSTEM unit=q2pen system=stores state=failed`,
#                   then `nav WP_REACHED unit=q2pen` with no `pilot ATTACK_RELEASE` after it
#   telemetry_q2pen.csv  sms_loaded stays 2, sms_released stays 0
#
# READING RULE: exit 3 = TIMEOUT is the EXPECTED verdict and is not the measurement - two `kill unit`
# objectives go unmet by design, one because the pickle was refused and one because the aeroplane that
# should have pressed it had no stores system left. THE MEASUREMENT IS THE FIVE-ROW TABLE ABOVE. A run
# in which `q2pen` is SHOT DOWN instead is a different and weaker result and must be reported as such.

net kari2
  control k2nod
  link wire
  period 4.0
  hold 3
  wcs free
  member k2nod
  member k2sa2 autonomy hold
  member k2sa3 autonomy hold
  member k2flk autonomy hold

unit q2str
  module f16
  team friendly
  spawn 33.20000 43.35000 5000 90.0 450
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 70
  set fcr_mode off
  set rwr on
  set store 3 mk84
  set store 7 mk84
  set brief_master_arm sim                      # THE ONE TOKEN. Its control reads `arm`.
  set task attack
  set attack_mode ccrp
  wp 33.20000 43.60000 5000 450
  wp 33.20000 43.10000 5000 450
  objective kill unit k2nod
  objective survive

unit q2pen
  module f16
  team friendly
  spawn 33.10000 43.30000 5000 90.0 450
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 80
  set fcr_mode off
  set rwr on
  set cmds_mode auto
  set cmds_program 1
  set cmds_chaff 60
  set cmds_flare 60
  set store 3 mk84
  set store 7 mk84
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task attack
  set attack_mode ccrp
  wp 33.10000 44.42000 5000 450
  wp 33.10000 43.90000 5000 450
  objective kill unit k2dra
  objective survive

unit k2nod
  module p18
  team hostile
  spawn 33.20000 43.60000 ground 0.0 0
  set emcon free

unit k2sa2
  module sa2
  team hostile
  spawn 33.14000 44.32000 ground 0.0 0
  set emcon hold
  set rounds 6

unit k2sa3
  module sa3
  team hostile
  spawn 33.06000 44.44000 ground 0.0 0
  set emcon hold
  set rounds 4

unit k2flk
  module zsu23
  team hostile
  spawn 33.20000 44.51000 ground 0.0 0
  set emcon hold
  set rounds 40

unit k2dra
  module target_soft
  team hostile
  spawn 33.10000 44.42000 ground 0.0 0

unit k2hq
  module target_soft
  team hostile
  spawn 33.26000 44.36000 ground 0.0 0

unit k2twa
  module target_hard
  team hostile
  spawn 33.20000 44.52000 ground 0.0 0
